  "CI_scope": "18 exact-head check-run metadata rows only: {\"cancelled\": 2, \"in_progress\": 2, \"queued\": 2, \"success\": 12}. No job logs or numerical runtime verification; repeated check names retained.",
  "fact": [
    "Public API validates NVIDIA CUDA, FP16/BF16/FP32 square logits1<=N<=8 and positive integer iterations. Output is FP32; input gradient returns input dtype; once_differentiable excludes higher-order autograd.",
    "Triton/Gluon/TileLang wrappers allocate history(2*iterations,M,N,N) FP32 iff grad enabled and logits requires_grad. M is the product of leading dimensions, not necessarily sequence length. Saved output is separate.",
    "Custom autograd retains the backward callable returned by the selected forward wrapper. Backward reverses the finite row/column normalization sequence.",
    "Tests compare outputs/VJPs to the same finite naive reference and assert row sums. They do not establish exact double stochasticity; non-NVIDIA and unavailable optional backends skip.",
    "Unified benchmark input TensorSpec defaults requires_grad=True, logits FP32. fwd callable does not disable autograd. The default fwd label therefore includes history allocation; it is not no-grad inference."
  ],
